<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91283" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτωτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτῶσις</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>capable of inflexion</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρθρον ἐστὶ στοιχεῖον λόγου
			π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Diog.Bab.Stoic.
				3.214
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνομά ἐστι μέρος λόγου
			π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				D.T.
				634.11
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				9.5
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ π. τὸ
			"Σωκράτης</span>" the <i>case-form</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σ</span>., <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				8.84
			</span></i>; <i>connected with cases</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π.
				σχῆμα</span>, when several cases of the same Noun follow one
			another, <i><span class="en">
				Simp.
				<u>in Cat.</u>
				359.9
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς, ἀντωνυμίαι κάτωθεν μὲν π.
					κινοῦνται ἄνωθεν δὲ προσωπικῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Choerob.
					<u>in Theod.</u>
					2.418
				</span></i>
			 H. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Math.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτωτικόν, τό</span>, <i>special case</i> of a problem, <i><span class="en">
				Papp.
				850.19
			</span></i>, al.</div>
